s, one for each of the coordinates."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4f0ce285448cf5a5048d4065","time_limit":40},{"id":"la_batch13_hyperplane_001_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $\\boldsymbol{a}\\neq\\boldsymbol{0}$ in $\\mathbb{R}^n$ and $d\\in\\mathbb{R}$. What is the intersection of the closed half-spaces $\\{\\boldsymbol{x}\\colon\\boldsymbol{a}\\cdot\\boldsymbol{x}\\le d\\}$ and $\\{\\boldsymbol{x}\\colon\\boldsymbol{a}\\cdot\\boldsymbol{x}\\ge d\\}$?","options":["The hyperplane $\\boldsymbol{a}\\cdot\\boldsymbol{x}=d$","The empty set","All of $\\mathbb{R}^n$","The line through $\\boldsymbol{0}$ spanned by $\\boldsymbol{a}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4acf4fcd24da17ed0de7ef92","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch13_hyperplane_020_curated20261027_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"In $\\mathbb{R}^2$, how are the hyperplanes $x+y=1$ and $2x+2y=2$ related?","options":["They are the same line.","They are parallel, distinct lines.","They meet in exactly one point.","They are perpendicular lines."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a9f0cedaa9df0d11a625dd3a","time_limit":20}]}}